u$ of $k$ there is a unique local point $x_{
u}\in ar{X}(k_{
u})$ associated with $s$. Since $s$ lifts to a b.l. section of $U$ by \autoref{tbb} and it is not geometric nor cuspidal, the set of places $
u$ such that $x_{
u}\in U$ has Dirichlet density $1$ by \cite[Theorem B]{sti15}, hence we may choose $
u$ with $x_{
u}\in U$ and $k'\subset k_{
u}$. If $r_{0,c}$ is a specialization of $r_{0}$ at $c$, by construction it is b.l. and lifts $s$, hence $r_{0,c,k_{
u}}$ is geometric associated with $x_{
u}$. By \autoref{uniqueloop1}, the specializing loop $S^{1}_{c}	o\Pi_{U_{k'}/k'}$ of $r_{0}$ at $c$ is constant and hence $r_{0}$ extends to a section $\spec\O_{c}	o\Pi_{U	imes{\mathbb A}^{1}/{\mathbb A}^{1}}$ by \autoref{prorootval}. Since we can do this for every closed point $c\in{\mathbb A}^{1}$ and we may write $\Pi_{U	imes{\mathbb A}^{1}/{\mathbb A}^{1}}$ as a product $\Pi_{U/k}	imes_{k}{\mathbb A}^{1}$, by \cite[Corollary A.3]{fed} we get that $r_{0}$ extends to a section $	ilde{r}_{0}:{\mathbb A}^{1}	o\Pi_{U	imes{\mathbb A}^{1}/{\mathbb A}^{1}}$. Since $\Pi_{{\mathbb A}^{1}/k}=\spec k$, the composition ${\mathbb A}^{1}	o\Pi_{U	imes{\mathbb A}^{1}/{\mathbb A}^{1}}	o\Pi_{U/k}$ factorizes through a section $r:\spec k	o\Pi_{U/k}$ and hence $	ilde{r}_{0}=r_{{\mathbb A}^{1}}$, $r_{0}=r_{k(t)}$. This implies that $r$ is a $t$-b.l. lifting of $s$. \end{proof}

